+# Q3 revenue drop
+
+East had the biggest percentage fall in revenue of any region from Q2 to Q3: it went from $333,747.57 to $234,325.08, down $99,422.49 or 29.79%. North was next at -4.33%. Most of East's fall came from Ledger Pro, whose revenue dropped from $106,520.77 to $23,015.24. That is a loss of $83,505.53, about 84% of the region's total drop. The cause was lower volume, not refunds or pricing: East sold roughly 150–185 Ledger Pro units a month in July–September, against 690–770 a month in Q2. Sales came back to 634 units in October. Revenue here is units × unit_price over completed rows only, with refunds (negative units) included.
+
+| Quarter | East revenue |
+|---------|-------------:|
+| Q1 | $333,565.48 |
+| Q2 | $333,747.57 |
+| Q3 | $234,325.08 |
+| Q4 | $305,168.76 |
